{"cells":[{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"d248588b","metadata":{"id":"d248588b"},"source":["# HR Analytics: Predicting Employee Attrition & Modeling Compensation\n","\n","** Machine Learning project e**\n","\n",.  \n","Every cell explains *what* we are doing, *why* we are doing it, and *what to look at* in the output.\n","\n","---\n","\n","### The business problem (say this in interviews)\n","\n","A company does not only want pretty charts. It wants answers:\n","\n","1. **Classification (Supervised):** Will this employee **leave** the company? (`Attrition = Yes/No`)\n","2. **Regression (Supervised):** What **monthly salary** is reasonable for this employee? (`MonthlyIncome`)\n","3. **Unsupervised:** Do employees fall into **natural groups**? (PCA + K-Means)\n","\n","We will solve all three on **one dataset**, using **only the algorithms i have studied**.\n","\n","### Dataset\n","\n","IBM HR Analytics Employee Attrition (1,470 employees, 35 columns).  \n","It is a well-known public dataset created by IBM. We load it from the internet — no Kaggle account needed.\n","\n","### How to run (Google Colab)\n","\n","1. Click **Runtime → Run all**\n","2. Wait 1–3 minutes\n","3. Scroll and read the printed explanations under each chart\n","\n","Run cells **in order from top to bottom**. Do not skip.\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"06cc581f","metadata":{"id":"06cc581f"},"source":["## Cell 1 — Import libraries\n","\n","Think of libraries as **toolboxes**:\n","\n","| Library | Job |\n","|---|---|\n","| `pandas` | Tables (like Excel, but in Python) |\n","| `numpy` | Numbers and arrays |\n","| `matplotlib` / `seaborn` | Charts |\n","| `sklearn` (scikit-learn) | Machine learning models and metrics |\n","\n","If this cell fails, click **Runtime → Restart session** and run it again.\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":1,"id":"9167ae61","metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"id":"9167ae61","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1787223321661,"user_tz":-