onstant) =====\")\n","print(df.nunique().sort_values())\n","\n","print(\"\\n===== TARGET 1 (Classification): Attrition =====\")\n","print(df[\"Attrition\"].value_counts())\n","print(\"Percentages:\")\n","print((df[\"Attrition\"].value_counts(normalize=True) * 100).round(2))\n","\n","print(\"\\n===== TARGET 2 (Regression): MonthlyIncome =====\")\n","print(df[\"MonthlyIncome\"].describe())\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"cfa468aa","metadata":{"id":"cfa468aa"},"source":["## Cell 4 — Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA)\n","\n","We draw charts to **see patterns with our eyes** before we ask a model.\n","\n","Things we want to notice:\n","- Attrition is **imbalanced** (many more \"No\" than \"Yes\"). Accuracy alone will look high even for a silly model that always says \"No\".\n","- Overtime, job role, and income often matter for leaving a job.\n","- Monthly income is **right-skewed** (a few people earn much more than the rest).\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":4,"id":"126e4b03","metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":1000},"id":"126e4b03","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1787223356591,"user_tz":-330,"elapsed":1648,"user":{"displayName":"Aryan Choudhary","userId":"07944419665814199827"}},"outputId":"8ab2f38c-f7af-4f4f-ecd2-7b6d3452d906"},"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 1400x1000 with 4 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}},{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["\n","Attrition rate by Department:\n","Attrition                 No   Yes\n","Department                        \n","Human Resources         81.0  19.0\n","Research & Development  86.2  13.8\n","Sales                   79.4  20.6\n","\n","Attrition rate by JobRole (highest first):\n","JobRole\n","Sales Representative         39.8\n","Laboratory Technician        23.9\n","Human Resources              23.1\n","Sales Executive              17.5\n","Research Scientist           16.1\n","Manufacturing Director        6.9\n","Healthcare Representative     6.9\n","Manager                       4.9\n","Research Director             2.5\n","Name: Yes, dtype: float64\n","\n","💡 Typical insight you may see:\n"," - People who work overtime leave more often.\n"," - Lower income employees leave more often.\n"," - Some roles (often Sales Representative) have much higher attrition.\n"]}],"source":["fig, axes = plt.subplots(2, 2, figsize=(14, 10))\n","\n","# 1. Attrition counts\n","sns.countplot(data=df, x=\"Attrition\", ax=axes[0, 0], palette=[\"#4caf50\", \"#e53935\"])\n","axes[0, 0].set_title(\"Who left vs who stayed?\")\n","for p in axes[0, 0].patches:\n","    axes[0, 0].annotate(int(p.get_height()), (p.get_x() + p.get_width() / 2, p.get_height()),\n","                        ha=\"center\", va=\"bottom\")\n","\n","# 2. Income by attrition\n","sns.boxplot(data=df, x=\"Attrition\", y=\"MonthlyIncome\", ax=axes[0, 1], palette=[\"#4caf50\", \"#e53935\"])\n","axes[0, 1].set_title(\"Monthly income vs attrition\")\n","\n","# 3. Overtime vs attrition (percent)\n","ot = pd.crosstab(df[\"OverTime\"], df[\"Attrition\"], normalize=\"index\") * 100\n","ot.plot(kind=\"bar\", stacked=True, ax=axes[1, 0], color=[\"#4caf50\", \"#e53935\"], legend=True)\n","axes[1, 0].set_title(\"Attrition % by overtime\")\n","axes[1, 0].set_ylabel(\"Percent of employees\")\n","axes[1, 0].tick_params(axis=\"x\", rotation=0)\n","\n","# 4. Age distribution\n","sns.histplot(data=df, x=\"Age\", hue=\"Attrition\", bins=20, kde=True, ax=axes[1, 1], palette=[\"#e53935\", \"#4caf50\"])\n","axes[1, 1].set_title(\"Age distribution by attrition\")\n","\n","plt.tight_layout()\n","plt.show()\n","\n","print(\"\\nAttrition rate by Department:\")\n","print((pd.crosstab(df[\"Department\"], df[\"Attrition\"], normalize=\"index\") * 100).round(1))\n","\n","print(\"\\nAttrition rate by JobRole (highest first):\")\n","role_attr = (pd.crosstab(df[\"JobRole\"], df[\"Attrition\"], normalize=\"index\") * 100)[\"Yes\"].sort_values(ascending=False)\n","print(role_attr.round(1))\n","\n","print(\"\\n💡 Typical insight you may see:\")\n","print(\" - People who work overtime leave more often.\")\n","print(\" - Lower income employees leave more often.\")\n","print(\" - Some roles (often Sales Representative) have much higher attrition.\")\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":5,"id":"027c90cf","metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":1000},"id":"027c90cf","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1787223370095,"user_tz":-330,"elapsed":2426,"user":{"displayName":"Aryan Choudhary","userId":"07944419665814199827"}},"outputId":"8c566a04-9ba8-4f58-e1f8-17e1438d5d6d"},"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 1600x1200 with 2 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}},{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["Top numeric correlations with MonthlyIncome:\n","MonthlyIncome              1.000000\n","JobLevel                   0.950300\n","TotalWorkingYears          0.772893\n","YearsAtCompany             0.514285\n","Age                        0.497855\n","YearsInCurrentRole         0.363818\n","YearsSinceLastPromotion    0.344978\n","YearsWithCurrManager       0.344079\n","Name: MonthlyIncome, dtype: float64\n"]}],"source":["# Correlation heatmap of numeric columns — helps later with feature selection\n","numeric_cols = df.select_dtypes(include=[np.number]).columns.tolist()\n","# Drop columns that are IDs or constants so the heatmap is readable\n","drop_from_corr = [c for c in [\"EmployeeCount\", \"EmployeeNumber\", \"StandardHours\"] if c in numeric_cols]\n","corr = df[numeric_cols].drop(columns=drop_from_corr).corr()\n","\n","plt.figure(figsize=(16, 12))\n","sns.heatmap(corr, cmap=\"vlag\", center=0, linewidths=0.3)\n","plt.title(\"Correlation heatmap (numeric features)\")\n","plt.tight_layout()\n","plt.show()\n","\n","print(\"Top numeric correlations with MonthlyIncome:\")\n","print(corr[\"MonthlyIncome\"].abs().sort_values(ascending=False).head(8))\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"d0aed69d","metadata":{"id":"d0aed69d"},"source":["## Cell 5 — ML Fundamentals (using THIS dataset)\n","\n","### Supervised vs Unsupervised — in one sentence each\n","\n","- **Supervised learning:** we already know the answer for past employees, and we want to predict it for new ones.\n","  - Example A: we know who left (`Attrition`) → classification\n","  - Example B: we know salary (`MonthlyIncome`) → regression\n","- **Unsupervised learning:** we do **not** give the model an answer. It only looks for structure.\n","  - Example: \"group similar employees\" with K-Means, or \"compress 30 columns into 2\" with PCA\n","\n","### Bias–variance tradeoff — in plain English\n","\n","Imagine studying for an exam:\n","\n","| Problem | School analogy | ML name | Typical fix |\n","|---|---|---|---|\n","| Model is too simple, misses the pattern | Memorized only 1 formula, scores low on every test | **High bias (underfitting)** | More features, a more flexible model |\n","| Model is too complex, memorizes noise | Memorized last year's paper word-for-word, fails a new paper | **High variance (overfitting)** | More data, simpler model, **regularization** (Ridge/Lasso), shallower trees |\n","\n","We will **see this live** later:\n","- Polynomial degree 1 vs degree 8 (regression)\n","- A shallow Decision Tree vs a very deep one (classification)\n","- Learning curves (train score vs test score as we add more data)\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":6,"id":"669e2a03","metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"id":"669e2a03","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1787223379736,"user_tz":-330,"elapsed":125,"user":{"displayName":"Aryan Choudhary","userId":"07944419665814199827"}},"outputId":"04ae9ab7-f4b6-4e17-b839-4494b3a0c532"},"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["SUPERVISED example from this table:\n","  X (inputs)  = Age, OverTime, JobRole, DistanceFromHome, ...\n","  y (answer)  = Attrition   → this is CLASSIFICATION because the answer is a label\n","  y (answer)  = MonthlyIncome → this is REGRESSION because the answer is a number\n","\n","UNSUPERVISED example from this table:\n","  We throw away Attrition and MonthlyIncome and ask:\n","  'Are there clusters of similar employees?'\n","\n","Class imbalance reminder:\n","  Only 16.1% employees left.\n","  A dummy model that always predicts 'No' already gets\n","  accuracy ≈ 83.9%  ← this is why we also use Precision, Recall, F1, ROC-AUC.\n"]}],"source":["print(\"SUPERVISED example from this table:\")\n","print(\"  X (inputs)  = Age, OverTime, JobRole, DistanceFromHome, ...\")\n","print(\"  y (answer)  = Attrition   → this is CLASSIFICATION because the answer is a label\")\n","print(\"  y (answer)  = MonthlyIncome → this is REGRESSION because the answer is a number\")\n","print()\n","print(\"UNSUPERVISED example from this table:\")\n","print(\"  We throw away Attrition and MonthlyIncome and ask:\")\n","print(\"  'Are there clusters of similar employees?'\")\n","print()\n","print(\"Class imbalance reminder:\")\n","yes_pct = (df[\"Attrition\"] == \"Yes\").mean() * 100\n","print(f\"  Only {yes_pct:.1f}% employees left.\")\n","print(\"  A dummy model that always predicts 'No' already gets\")\n","print(f\"  accuracy ≈ {100 - yes_pct:.1f}%  ← this is why we also use Precision, Recall, F1, ROC-AUC.\")\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"bc13fade","metadata":{"id":"bc13fade"},"source":["## Cell 6 — Data cleaning\n","\n","Cleaning = removing things that **cannot help a model** or that **leak the answer**.\n","\n","We drop:\n","- `EmployeeNumber` → just an ID, like a roll number\n","- `EmployeeCount`, `Over18`, `StandardHours` → they have **only 1 unique value** (zero information)\n","- `DailyRate`, `HourlyRate`, `MonthlyRate` → other pay figures that are almost another version of salary.  \n","  If we keep them, salary prediction becomes cheating, and attrition models get confused by duplicate pay info.\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":7,"id":"189ba3bf","metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"id":"189ba3bf","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1787223388382,"user_tz":-330,"elapsed":118,"user":{"displayName":"Aryan Choudhary","userId":"07944419665814199827"}},"outputId":"3c08fbaa-eaab-4db1-b469-531ea9766339"},"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["Unique values in the constant-looking columns:\n","  EmployeeCount: [1]\n","  Over18: ['Y']\n","  StandardHours: [80]\n","\n","Shape before cleaning: (1470, 35)\n","Shape after cleaning : (1470, 28)\n","Columns left:\n"," ['Age', 'Attrition', 'BusinessTravel', 'Department', 'DistanceFromHome', 'Education', 'EducationField', 'EnvironmentSatisfaction', 'Gender', 'JobInvolvement', 'JobLevel', 'JobRole', 'JobSatisfaction', 'MaritalStatus', 'MonthlyIncome', 'NumCompaniesWorked', 'OverTime', 'PercentSalaryHike', 'PerformanceRating', 'RelationshipSatisfaction', 'StockOptionLevel', 'TotalWorkingYears', 'TrainingTimesLastYear', 'WorkLifeBalance', 'YearsAtCompany', 'YearsInCurrentRole', 'YearsSinceLastPromotion', 'YearsWithCurrManager']\n","\n","✅ Cleaning done. Original df is unchanged; we work with df_clean from now on.\n"]}],"source":["print(\"Unique values in the constant-looking columns:\")\n","for col in [\"EmployeeCount\", \"Over18\", \"StandardHours\"]:\n","    print(f\"  {col}: {df[col].unique()}\")\n","\n","df_clean = df.drop(columns=[\n","    \"EmployeeNumber\", \"EmployeeCount\", \"Over18\", \"StandardHours\",\n","    \"DailyRate\", \"HourlyRate\", \"MonthlyRate\",\n","])\n","\n","print(\"\\nShape before cleaning:\", df.shape)\n","print(\"Shape after cleaning :\", df_clean.shape)\n","print(\"Columns left:\\n\", list(df_clean.columns))\n","print(\"\\n✅ Cleaning done. Original df is unchanged; we work with df_clean from now on.\")\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"9042f740","metadata":{"id":"9042f740"},"source":["## Cell 7 — Feature Engineering\n","\n","**Feature engineering** means turning raw columns into better inputs.\n","\n","We will do all four skills from your list:\n","\n","1. **Transformation** — create new columns (ratios, log of skewed numbers)\n","2. **Encoding** — convert text (Yes/No, Department) into numbers\n","3. **Scaling** — put numbers on a similar scale (important for KNN, SVM, Linear/Ridge/Lasso)\n","4. **Selection** — keep the most useful columns, drop noisy ones\n","\n","### Important rule (leakage)\n","- For **salary regression**, `MonthlyIncome` is the *answer*, so it cannot be a feature.\n","- `JobLevel` is almost a salary grade. We **keep** it for attrition, but we will also show a fairer salary model **without** `JobLevel` so the model is not just reading the pay band.\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":8,"id":"3abe00e9","metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":365},"id":"3abe00e9","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1787223405472,"user_tz":-330,"elapsed":260,"user":{"displayName":"Aryan Choudhary","userId":"07944419665814199827"}},"outputId":"2d3b88aa-625b-46f7-c83c-f3b48d601f15"},"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["New engineered columns (first 5 rows):\n"]},{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["   TenureRatio  AgeWhenStarted  YearsPerCompany  AvgSatisfaction  LogDistanceFromHome\n","0     0.666667              33         0.888889             2.00             0.693147\n","1     0.909091              39         5.000000             3.00             2.197225\n","2     0.000000              30         1.000000             3.00             1.098612\n","3     0.888889              25         4.000000             3.25             1.386294\n","4     0.285714              21         0.600000             2.50             1.098612"],"text/html":["\n","  <div id=\"df-1444d677-69bf-47d5-bcae-9e543a105597\" class=\"colab-df-container\">\n","    <div>\n","<style scoped>\n","    .dataframe tbody tr th:only-of-type {\n","        vertical-align: mid